{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Send, gather your livestock.</b> But had they not already died in the plague of pestilence? And the verse testifies there accordingly: ״וימת כל מקנה מצרים״ (Exodus 9:6). Perhaps this livestock they had brought from other lands, and the people of Egypt had purchased it from them, and concerning this Moses now commanded that they gather it indoors. Or the sense of ״וימת כל מקנה מצרים״ may be the majority of the livestock, for the majority is as the whole. Or it is possible that ״וימת כל מקנה מצרים״ means all livestock in which Israel had no partnership — but that which was jointly held with Israel is what was saved from the plague of pestilence."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:15.025637076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}